From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Lopez <norelec@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:58:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Run plugins on .NET 10 inside the client instead of Mono

The client is a NativeAOT executable, so CUO_API plugins such as Razor
Enhanced, built for .NET Framework, need a runtime to run on. Upstream used a
.NET Framework bootstrap on Windows and Mono (monokickstart) elsewhere; both go.

When settings.json lists plugins, CoreClrPluginHost.cs finds hostfxr and starts
the .NET 10 runtime in the client's process, then loads ClassicUO.PluginHost.dll
(from the old Bootstrap sources). It fills the HostBindings table the bootstrap
used to hand over, so the client side is unchanged from upstream. Plugins go
into the host's load context, the entry assembly is set to the host, and their
dependencies are found next to each plugin. Without plugins nothing starts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LFcBNQtF3Z7vfzi99BXwUe
